<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- **Jaro came off this list on 2026-10-01, and out of the bundle with it.**

	     It was registering a face no Swift read. `JaroFont` was deleted for the
	     second time (`Typography.swift`, MARK: - Jaro, which records the first
	     one on 2026-09-09), the wordmark went on 2026-09-30 and the mark is the
	     pre-drawn `StrataSMark` asset, which carries no font at all. The sweep
	     that found it could not finish the job because it could not prove
	     nothing outside Swift named the family. That is now proved, by grep over
	     the whole tree: no `.custom(` anywhere, no `UIFont(name:)` or
	     `CTFontCreateWithName` except `StrataFont`'s own two, which name
	     "Strata-Regular"; no .xib and no .storyboard in the repo at all; nothing
	     in `Strata/Assets.xcassets` mentions a font; and the only other target,
	     the widget, has its own `WidgetSupport/Info.plist` registering
	     Strata-Regular alone. There is no Intents extension.

	     The 145,616 bytes are gone too, which the plist alone would not have
	     done: the target is a file-system-synchronized group, so every non-source
	     file under `Strata/` ships, and the file is excluded by a
	     `PBXFileSystemSynchronizedBuildFileExceptionSet` in `project.pbxproj`.

	     **The TTF itself stays in the repo and must.** `tools/make_app_icon.py`
	     and `tools/make_logo.py` read `Strata/Resources/Jaro.ttf` to derive the
	     icon and the `S` offline, and `Jaro-OFL.txt` stays beside it. Moving the
	     file out of the target directory would have been the other way to do
	     this, and it was not taken: it means editing two tools that are not
	     this change's to edit, for the same bytes.

	     `Jaro-OFL.txt` is deliberately left in the bundle. It is 4.4 KB and
	     the SIL licence's requirements are about distributing the FONT, which
	     this build no longer does, so taking it out is a legal call rather
	     than a cleanup and nobody asked for one. -->
	<key>UIAppFonts</key>
	<array>
		<string>Strata-Regular.ttf</string>
	</array>
	<key>UILaunchScreen</key>
	<dict>
		<key>UIColorName</key>
		<string>LaunchBlack</string>
	</dict>
	<key>UTExportedTypeDeclarations</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>UTTypeConformsTo</key>
			<array>
				<string>public.data</string>
			</array>
			<key>UTTypeDescription</key>
			<string>Strata Block</string>
			<key>UTTypeIdentifier</key>
			<string>co.strataapp.blockmove</string>
		</dict>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
